# Memory-path migration aliases (#177).
#
# When a plugin restructure renames an internal path, add an `old -> new`
# mapping here so memory files that still reference the OLD path pass
# pre-commit-hooks/memory-drift-check.sh: the gate treats a stale OLD
# reference as live when its mapped NEW path resolves (index / worktree /
# external root). This is the documented migration mechanism — preferable to
# hand-editing every affected memory file or papering over the gap with
# MEMORY_DRIFT_EXTERNAL_ROOTS.
#
# Format: one `old -> new` mapping per line; `#` comments and blank lines are
# ignored. An `old` that ENDS IN `/` is a PREFIX rename (rewrites the prefix,
# keeps the remainder); any other `old` is matched EXACTLY (a bare segment is
# never a broad prefix). First match wins. Paths are repo-relative (the same
# form memory files reference).
#
# Skills live at the plugin's top-level `skills/X/run.sh`, but memory written
# against the consumer layout references `.claude/skills/X/run.sh`; this prefix
# rename keeps those references resolving.
.claude/skills/ -> skills/

# The consumer override scaffold `.claude/local-overrides.yml` is generated
# from the plugin's template; memory (Wave G #232) references the consumer
# path. Map it to the plugin-source template so the reference resolves.
.claude/local-overrides.yml -> templates/local-overrides.yml.tpl
